/* ReverseArray_r: intermediate level of ReverseArray, written by hand (PipelineB, refinement step),
   the component BART refines.
   Purpose: replace the lambda of reverse by the facts a loop establishes: the new array is a total
   function, and each position holds the value of its mirror position. The proof that these facts
   define the lambda (equality of two functions) is thus done once, here, away from the loop.
   array stays the concrete variable of ReverseArray, and its initialisation is unchanged.
   Same shape as FillArray_r and Quicksort_r, the levels with an inherited concrete variable BART
   has refined: an INVARIANT clause restating the type of array, and an ANY, taken by a structure
   rule, in place of a becomes-such-that on the variable itself. */
REFINEMENT
    ReverseArray_r

REFINES
    ReverseArray

SEES
    Ctx_ReverseArray

INVARIANT
    array : (0..max_IDX) --> INT

INITIALISATION
    array := %ii.(ii : 0..max_IDX | ii)

OPERATIONS

    reverse =
    ANY rr WHERE
        rr : (0..max_IDX) --> INT &
        !ii.(ii : 0..max_IDX => rr(ii) = array(max_IDX - ii))
    THEN
        array := rr
    END

END
